# Cloudflare Pages redirect rules (first match wins, evaluated before asset lookup).
#
# Two separate concerns live here; only one is expressible in this file.
#
# 1. Legacy duplicate-intent routes (below) — the 8 permanent 301s ported from
#    vercel.json. Every target is a real prerendered page, verified by
#    scripts/audit-domain-migration.ts.
#
# 2. Host-level canonicalisation — NOT expressible here. Cloudflare `_redirects`
#    matches paths on the host that serves the file; it cannot match "the apex
#    host". The apex totalcalculation.com -> www.totalcalculation.com redirect is
#    a Cloudflare Redirect Rule on the zone, and it MUST preserve the path and the
#    query string. The rule that shipped first dropped both and sent every apex
#    URL to the homepage. See docs/domain-migration-audit.md §5 for the exact
#    expression and the verification check.
#
# Do not add a catch-all `/* https://www.totalcalculation.com/:splat` rule here:
# this same file is served on the www host, so that rule would loop.
#
# Verified live 2026-10-30: https://totalcalculation.com/about 301 ->
# https://www.totalcalculation.com (path NOT preserved — owner action required).

/calculators/mortgage-payment-calculator /calculators/mortgage-calculator 301
